# Senior Change Lifecycle (Mandatory)

Follow this sequence before and after every code update.

## 1) Understand First
- Restate the requirement in clear, testable terms.
- Confirm scope, constraints, and expected behavior.
- If any requirement is ambiguous, ask before coding.

## 2) Pre-Change Impact Check
- Identify affected files, flows, APIs, data, and edge cases.
- Check what can break (UI, logic, validations, integrations, performance).
- Define acceptance criteria and regression checklist.

## 3) Safe Implementation
- Apply smallest safe change that satisfies the requirement.
- Preserve existing behavior unless change explicitly requires it.
- Add/adjust focused comments only where logic is non-obvious.

## 4) Focused Error Handling
- Report only actionable root-cause errors and critical pain points.
- Avoid noisy or generic error reporting.
- Include precise context needed for quick fixes.

## 5) Triple Validation
- Verify correctness of the new behavior.
- Verify no functional regressions in related flows.
- Verify no visual regressions in affected screens/components.

## 6) QA Gate Before Handoff
- Run relevant checks/tests available in project workflow.
- Manually test key user scenarios and edge cases.
- Hand off only after all checks pass or clearly document any blocker/risk.

## 7) Final Delivery Format
- Provide: what changed, why, impact area, validation done, and residual risks.
- Never mark work complete without lifecycle and QA confirmation.
